  "dietSummary": "Mostly fed by the algae in its tissue; catches mysis, krill and pellets with sticky tentacles and passes them to its mouth. A meaty feed once or twice a week helps it grow.",
  "temperamentSummary": "Walks on its foot until it finds a crevice with good light and flow, then stays. Stings corals and fish it touches, except clownfish that have adopted it.",
  "careNotes": [
    "Add to a mature tank (6+ months); keep it away from powerhead intakes.",
    "Tentacles swell into bubbles or go long and stringy; the cause is not well understood (light and feeding are suspects).",
    "Deflates now and then to flush waste and reinflates over a few hours; daily deflation or a gaping mouth means trouble.",
    "Bleaches (turns pale) after several days above about 27-28 C, faster under strong light.",
    "Can split in two (clones); clones sit together peacefully but sting other anemones.",
    "Ocellaris clowns are not natural hosts but usually adopt it after days to weeks of testing touches."
